id: pm-web-jpa6
title: GET graph installs or activates pm-graph and bypasses edit permission
description: "GET /api/projects/:projectId/pm/graph calls pmGraphExtensionGraphForProject, which calls ensureGraphExtension. The helper can install npm:pm-graph and activate it, so a safe-method request mutates project state. The pm router's permission middleware exempts GET/HEAD/OPTIONS, which also lets view-only collaborators trigger the mutation. This was found while tracing the complete CSRF boundary for pm-web-413z and must be repaired as a distinct route-semantics/authorization change."
type: Issue
pm_format_version: 2
status: closed
priority: 0
tags[4]: authorization,http-semantics,pm-graph,security
created_at: "2026-08-30T20:58:12.273Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T19:43:58.139Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-21T19:43:57.041Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-21T19:43:57.041Z"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "GET /pm/graph is observational and never installs, activates, or otherwise mutates an extension; any explicit provisioning uses a CSRF-protected unsafe method and requires edit permission; view-only users can read the fallback graph without changing project state; real route tests prove command logs remain mutation-free on GET."
why_now: A state-changing GET can be triggered cross-origin and currently bypasses the edit-permission middleware by design.
reviewer: security-review
risk: high
confidence: high
reporter: codex
severity: high
environment: pm-web 2026.8.29 at 7e09ca9
repro_steps: "Request GET /api/projects/:projectId/pm/graph for a project without active pm-graph; pmGraphExtensionGraphForProject calls ensureGraphExtension, which runs pm install and extension activate."
resolution: "Reverified main ca7e188bc91e (unchanged since audit): [PR #206](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/206) (cae97c5) makes graph GET observational and moves provisioning to an editor/CSRF-protected POST; real route tests assert no GET mutation. Retained evidence: public/src/views/graph.ts, src/routes/pm.ts, src/services/pm-runner.ts."
expected_result: GET reads the installed graph when available or returns the fallback graph without mutation.
actual_result: "GET may install and activate pm-graph, including for view-only users."
affected_version: 2026.8.29
component: Graph HTTP routes
customer_impact: Cross-origin or view-only callers can change a project's extension state through a nominally read-only endpoint.
comments[18]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-02T23:39:10.654Z",codex-sol,"Correction to historical 2026-09-26 notes: the neighbors activation route was a separate follow-up then, and is now implemented by ae65f73 within PR #161. pm-web-24fc tracks its remaining response-parity and independent acceptance gates. Only pm-web-38n5 is the pure extension-export fidelity follow-up. All dated notes/history are retained; neither issue is closed and no hosted acceptance is claimed."
  "2026-10-03T00:05:07.319Z",claude-orchestrator,"Unblocked 2026-10-03 (cubic review on PR #161): this item's own acceptance is implemented in PR #161 (GET /pm/graph and neighbors are observational, provisioning needs an unsafe CSRF-protected method with edit permission, route tests assert mutation-free command logs). The 'blocked' status reflected repo-wide gates, not this defect: pm-web's whole-source coverage below 100 is tracked by pm-web-ulgy (routes/pm.ts and bootstrap) and pm-web-9ulj (route layer on real Postgres); extension-native response parity is pm-web-38n5. Close after PR #161 merges."
  "2026-10-04T09:14:31.421Z",pi-land-s2,"Accepted Greptile 4170831675: the 2026-10-03 comment claimed the graph route tests assert mutation-free command logs, but the test only checked the activation marker, extension install dir, and settings. The graph read test now records a real command log: PM_CLI_BIN wraps the real pm and appends every spawned argv, and the test asserts the log has no mutation entries after the GET/HEAD/owner/neighbors read phase. Red-first proof: with the GET route temporarily reverted to the provisioning behavior (and a no-op stub pm), the assertion fails on 'install npm:pm-graph --project' and 'extension activate pm-graph --project' per GET; with the shipped observational route it passes unchanged. This makes the item's command-log acceptance criterion actually verified."
  "2026-10-04T10:14:37.361Z",pi-land-s2,"Greptile follow-up 4176981023 on the command-log regression: accepted. The three new previous-env restores were declared after the t.after hook registration and after risky fixture setup, so an early failure (e.g. pm init) would read them in teardown from the temporal dead zone, masking the original error and skipping workspace removal. The captures now sit with previousRoot/previousMarker at the top of the test, before the hook and before any risky call, matching the file's established pattern. Focused graph test passes unchanged."
  "2026-10-15T10:58:52.686Z",codex-agent,"Current main already uses the certified observational graph builder and preserves installed export parity without loading project extension hooks. Complete the remaining acceptance with a dedicated POST graph/provision behind global CSRF and router edit checks, editor-only enable control, static activation-state inspection, byte-identical settings/registry assertions, real provisioning idempotency, behavioural revert proof and built-server curl proof. Hosted deployment is outside scope."
  "2026-10-15T11:02:55.580Z",codex-agent,"Focused graph regression: 7/7 passed with real HTTP, PostgreSQL, disposable trackers and npm installer. Concurrent editor provisioning and a retry issued exactly one install; viewers, missing CSRF tokens and foreign-origin POSTs returned 403. GET selects installed pure export output only when configured enabled, otherwise fallback; neither read executes project code. Production proof: build plus NODE_ENV=production dist/server.js against disposable projects, curl anonymous 401, viewer 200, cross-origin viewer without CSRF 200; settings and registry SHA-256 byte identity preserved across all three requests. Reproducible proof helper: test/helpers/graph-production-proof.ts."
  "2026-10-15T11:03:28.194Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: temporarily added only await ensureGraphExtension(project.ownerUserId, project.slug) back to GET /graph, then ran node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test test/graph-provision.test.ts against the real installer. Result 0/1 passed, exit 1, AssertionError: GET must leave settings and extension registry byte-identical. Restored the observational route; identical regression passes 1/1. No SDK or installer mocks used."
  "2026-10-15T11:06:01.334Z",codex-agent,"PM runner gaps observed: the historical linked command was refused because its source branch differs; reviewed the exact command and acknowledged it for this clone. The expanded real-export suite exceeded the default 120-second linked-command limit (its 20-seed property case completed at 112 seconds); set an explicit 300-second timeout without altering assertions or package thresholds. Result tracking is disabled by existing policy, so pm test reports evidence_recording=false; retain sanitized outcomes in comments instead of changing project policy. Production linked proof passed. Will rerun all linked commands after the full gate."
  "2026-10-15T11:17:22.075Z",codex-agent,"Initial isolated npm release run used the catalog test's default sibling discovery, which sees the incomplete worktree collection. Catalog assertions reproduce 14/16 there and pass 16/16 with canonical fleet context through PM_FLEET_ROOT. Catalog implementation and tests are byte-unchanged from origin/main. Full run also hit the existing 300-second Presets aggregate timeout tracked by pm-web-qdhx (built case passed at 240.939 seconds). Rerun the complete gates sequentially with canonical fleet context and unchanged thresholds/deadlines."
  "2026-10-15T11:26:21.440Z",codex-agent,"PM-linked acceptance now passes 3/3 commands, including 7/7 graph tests and production curl proof; the final pinned-binary read-only regression also passes 1/1. First complete npm suite: 593 tests, 590 pass, 2 catalog discovery failures, 1 unchanged Presets deadline cancellation, zero skips/todo. Failed-run coverage measured statements/lines 90.87, branches 81.37, functions 94.13 and is not accepted gate evidence. Canonical fleet catalog alone passes 16/16. Begin one full npm retry with canonical fleet context, followed by the full Bun gate; all package thresholds and acceptance deadlines remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-15T11:45:36.439Z",codex-agent,"Canonical-fleet npm release retry remains red at coverage: 591/593 pass, one unchanged Presets aggregate timeout cancellation and its source-case spawn ENOTDIR failure, zero skips/todo. All graph tests and fleet assertions pass. Existing pm-web-qdhx records the exact failure boundary; coverage percentages exceed configured thresholds but are not accepted evidence from a failing suite. Full isolated Bun release gate now running with canonical fleet context; do not claim complete release certification."
  "2026-10-15T12:01:27.740Z",codex-agent,"Full isolated Bun release:check passes with canonical fleet context: 593/593 tests, zero fail/cancel/skip/todo; all 36 configured source files, S/L 90.85, B 81.28, F 94.13; zero production audit vulnerabilities; packed consumers 4/4 (npm/Bun current and minimum hosts); changelog/date/publish-attestation checks pass. The unchanged catalog cases passed at 237.128 seconds built and 213.116 seconds source. This new full green evidence justifies one more isolated npm run on unchanged code to resolve its remaining red gate, retaining both prior failures."
  "2026-10-15T12:14:16.409Z",codex-agent,"Final delivery evidence: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both exit 0 with isolated Git identity and canonical fleet context. Each suite passes 593/593, zero fail/cancel/skip/todo; each packed acceptance passes 4/4 current/minimum npm/Bun consumers, production audit reports zero vulnerabilities, duplication is zero clone pairs, and 647 declarations are documented. All 36 configured source files are covered: npm S/L 90.87, B 81.35, F 94.13; Bun S/L 90.85, B 81.28, F 94.13. Thresholds, acceptance deadlines and dependency pins are unchanged. Revert proof and built production curl proof are retained above; PM-linked commands pass 3/3. Preserve the earlier failed evidence and open timing follow-up pm-web-qdhx. Release the claim for review without closing this item; hosted deployment remains untouched."
  "2026-10-21T07:09:46.384Z",codex-agent,"Related receipt from pm-web-jstr: the unchanged CSRF-protected editor provisioning acceptance passed in the full npm coverage run but failed in the full Bun run. Both concurrent POST graph/provision requests returned HTTP 424 after roughly 140 seconds. Observational graph GET/HEAD tests passed in both runs. The dependency failure category has not been traced; no recurrence of the historical unsafe GET behavior is inferred. The dated join-storm report retains this separate release-gate failure."
  "2026-10-21T07:13:43.946Z",codex-agent,"Final Bun failure details identify activation as the failing phase: the real provisioning response was HTTP 424 with installed true, active false and a 30000 ms pm-command timeout. Both concurrent POSTs returned that outcome. The existing deprecated extension-command diagnostic was also present, but no causal diagnosis of the timeout was made. The full Bun runner finished 756 pass, four fail and one canceled out of 761. The dated report preserves this receipt; no route or runner change is included for this separate failure."
  "2026-10-21T19:25:46.693Z",codex-agent,"Reverified main ca7e188bc91e (unchanged since audit): [PR #206](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/206) (cae97c5) makes graph GET observational and moves provisioning to an editor/CSRF-protected POST; real route tests assert no GET mutation. Retained evidence: public/src/views/graph.ts, src/routes/pm.ts, src/services/pm-runner.ts."
  "2026-10-21T19:28:57.890Z",codex-agent,Refreshed open-PR references before continuing reconciliation. PR #236 now also references pm-web-jstr and pm-web-sspv; both remain untouched. The refreshed skip set contains nine items and leaves 37 eligible reconciliation entries. Existing duplicate links can still point to the canonical sspv item without closing it.
